WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:06.089
Who has seen
an advertisement

00:00:06.798 --> 00:00:09.718
that has convinced you
that your microphone

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.762
is listening
to your conversations?

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:16.475
All of your interactions,

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:17.976
your credit card swipes,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:18.977
web searches,

00:00:19.061 --> 00:00:20.896
locations, likes,

00:00:20.979 --> 00:00:22.898
they're all collected
in real time

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.859
into a trillion-dollar-a-year
industry.

00:00:27.319 --> 00:00:30.906
The real game-changer
was Cambridge Analytica.

00:00:31.365 --> 00:00:33.033
They've worked
for the Trump campaign

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:34.910
and for the Brexit campaign.

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:37.829
They started using
information warfare.

00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:39.122
Cambridge Analytica

00:00:39.206 --> 00:00:41.667
claimed to have
5,000 data points

00:00:41.959 --> 00:00:43.794
on every American voter.

00:00:46.338 --> 00:00:47.923
I started tracking down

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:50.926
all these Cambridge Analytica
ex-employees.

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:52.678
Someone else
you should be calling

00:00:52.761 --> 00:00:54.346
to the committee
is Brittany Kaiser.

00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:56.348
Brittany Kaiser,

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:59.059
once a key player
inside Cambridge Analytica,

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:01.061
casting herself
as a whistle-blower.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.855
The reason why Google
and Facebook

00:01:03.939 --> 00:01:05.899 line:0%
are the most powerful
companies in the world

00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:09.361 line:0%
is because last year,
data surpassed oil in value.

00:01:10.821 --> 00:01:13.282
It is the most valuable asset
on Earth.

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:15.701
We targeted those

00:01:15.784 --> 00:01:17.619
whose minds
we thought we could change,

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.455
until they saw the world
the way we wanted them to.

00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:24.418
I do know
that their targeting tool

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:25.752
was considered a weapon.

00:01:25.836 --> 00:01:27.087
There is a possibility

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.548
that the American public
have been experimented on.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.883
This is becoming
a criminal matter.

00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:34.344
When people see
the extent of the surveillance,

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:36.388
I think they're going
to be shocked.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:40.767
-And I still fear for your life.
-Yeah.

00:01:40.851 --> 00:01:42.686
With the powerful people
involved.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.855
But I can't keep quiet
just because&nbsp;it'll make

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.440
-powerful people mad.
-I know.

00:01:47.691 --> 00:01:48.525
Data rights

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:50.611
should be considered
just fundamental rights.

00:01:51.612 --> 00:01:54.406
This is about the integrity
of our democracy.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.368
These platforms which were
created to connect us

00:01:58.994 --> 00:02:01.330
have now been weaponized.

00:02:01.413 --> 00:02:04.249
It's impossible to know
what is what.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.337
Because nothing is
what it seems.

